@1101 = ~Quaramon the Devourer~
@1102 = ~Wahahahaha... Delicious!~
@1103 = ~The Monster's Candle~
@1104 = ~Katana +4~
@1105 = ~This candle was once given by the local healing priest to Bilan Bogel, a young farmer from Feathervale. Bilan often spoke of how his son, Gud, claimed that a great humanoid beast prowled about their home every night, though Bilan himself could see nothing at all. Convinced by the sincerity of his son's fears despite his own inability to perceive the intruder, Bilan sought the priest's aid. The priest entrusted him with this candle, assuring him that its light would dispel whatever illusion concealed the creature.
The candle worked exactly as promised.
That very night, Bilan finally beheld the monster: a towering ogre clad in gaudy, brightly colored garments. Before he could recover from his astonishment, the ogre uttered an incantation. A heartbeat later, Bilan was engulfed in flames, terribly wounded by the Fireball the creature had hurled at him. As he staggered back toward the farmhouse, he saw two enormous hands smash through the window, seize Gud, and disappear into the darkness. When Bilan emerged once more, neither the ogre nor his son was anywhere to be seen, though Gud's screams still echoed across the fields. He tried to follow the cries, but soon lost the trail.
The following night, Bilan lit the candle again. This time he came prepared, armed and accompanied by several fellow farmers. When the ogre once more became visible in the candlelight, they charged him without hesitation.
It was the last thing any of them ever did.
On the third day, the priest returned to reclaim the candle. Before long he would entrust it to someone else. And once every family had returned it, he would simply move on to another village...

STATISTICS:

Once per day, summons Quaramon the Devourer, a 5th-level Ogre Mage, for 3 turns.

Special Ability:
Quaramon can devour Ioun Stones. If his summoner possesses an Ioun Stone when Quaramon is called, he immediately takes the stone and returns to the candle to consume it. He may then be summoned again, having grown more powerful.

Each Ioun Stone consumed grants Quaramon:
• +3 Hit Points
• One additional memorized spell
For every two Ioun Stones consumed:
• +1 THAC0
• +1 Caster Level
For every three Ioun Stones consumed:
• +1 bonus to all Saving Throws
• One additional known spell.
For every five Ioun Stones consumed:
• +1 Armor Class
For every seven Ioun Stones consumed:
• Quaramon's katana gains +1 enchantment (its base enchantment is +1).

Current Statistics:

Hit Points: 45
THAC0: 15
Armor Class: 4
Weapon: Katana +1
Saving Throws: 11 / 13 / 12 / 13 / 14
Special Ability: Kai ×1
Caster Level: 5

Spells:
2× Charm Person
1× Sleep
1× Invisibility
1× Horror
1× Fireball~

